WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.475
Here's the loop the rest
of the path builds.

2
00:00:02.475 --> 00:00:05.135
Collect from the
provider, not the mailbox:

3
00:00:05.135 --> 00:00:09.315
a read-only identity reads each
provider's notices at least weekly,

4
00:00:09.315 --> 00:00:13.875
through the provider's own interface,
and each notice becomes one record.

5
00:00:13.875 --> 00:00:18.058
Route by rules, in order: security
advisories, then retirements,

6
00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:21.516
then maintenance that names
the agency's resources,

7
00:00:21.516 --> 00:00:26.825
then open incidents that name them, then
anything else marked as needing action.

8
00:00:26.825 --> 00:00:31.737
The first match wins, and a notice that
matches none goes to the weekly digest.

9
00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:36.509
A notice that needs action becomes a
typed task in the I T S M front door,

10
00:00:36.509 --> 00:00:40.862
not a second queue, with an owner,
a severity and response window,

11
00:00:40.862 --> 00:00:43.875
and the provider's own
date kept separately.

12
00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:46.221
It's keyed to the provider's notice I D,

13
00:00:46.221 --> 00:00:49.350
so an unchanged notice
never makes a second task.

14
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.339
And a task closes only on the
re-read: when the next collection

15
00:00:53.339 --> 00:00:57.887
shows the notice closed, or the
agency's resources no longer affected.

16
00:00:57.887 --> 00:01:00.639
A retirement can close
on the provider's side

17
00:01:00.639 --> 00:01:03.670
while the agency still
runs the retired version.
